From e782654028f5e32558d1fde7ca5b8eea74922007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:40:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] spi: airoha: allow dual and quad data phases in manual mode

airoha_spi_supports_op() only accepted a data phase wider than one wire
for the SPI-NAND page operations, so a SPI-NOR on the manual path always
fell back to single-wire reads. The manual FIFO already takes the data
phase at the width it is given, including the turnaround on the phase
before it, so accept 1-1-2 and 1-1-4 operations as well. The SPI core
still limits them to what the device's bus width allows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c
index ddfe1ceff..de2c91ac7 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-airoha-snfi.c
@@ -776,9 +776,12 @@ static bool airoha_spi_supports_op(struct spi_mem *mem,
 	if (airoha_spi_is_page_ops(op))
 		return true;
 
+	/*
+	 * The manual FIFO takes the data phase at the width it is given, so
+	 * 1-1-2 and 1-1-4 reads work as long as the device can do them.
+	 */
 	return (!op->addr.nbytes || op->addr.buswidth == 1) &&
-	       (!op->dummy.nbytes || op->dummy.buswidth == 1) &&
-	       (!op->data.nbytes || op->data.buswidth == 1);
+	       (!op->dummy.nbytes || op->dummy.buswidth == 1);
 }
 
 static int airoha_spi_exec_op(struct spi_mem *mem,
